  "hh_ethnologue_comment": {
    "comment": "E16/E17/E18/E19/E20/E21/E22/E23/E24/E25/E26/E27/E28/E29 has a Yokuts [yok] entry which subsumes ``many subvarieties''.\nHowever, careful analysis of all extant Yokutsan materials necessitate the division into several related languages, minimally adding three language-level entries (all extinct) to the one found in E16/E17/E18/E19/E20/E21/E22/E23/E24/E25/E26/E27/E28/E29, i.e., Palewyami Yokuts, Buena Vista Yokuts and Tule-Kaweah Yokuts. See also: Yokuts [yok].",
